  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum magnitude outcome weighted by its probability, which involves comparing 2500×0.33 and 2400×0.34. The individual explicitly considers both the higher outcome of A (2500 vs. 2400) and the probability difference (33% vs. 34%), noting that the probability is only 'one percent less' — which shows awareness of both components required by the reason. Although the individual does not explicitly perform the multiplication, the reasoning pattern aligns with evaluating the attractiveness of the top prize in relation to its likelihood. The justification centers on the same two variables (maximum outcome and its probability) and their relative trade-off, which matches the core logic of the decision reason. Therefore, the individual’s deliberation is consistent with using the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
